\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Operator spinors on a minimal left ideal}
\date{2026-11-12}

\p{Suppose the Clifford algebra of \ref{fdip-00O5} has a minimal left
ideal #{S}. Left multiplication is then an algebra homomorphism
#{\operatorname{Cl}(q_x)\to\operatorname{End}_k(S)}. Hestenes and
Sobczyk take an operator of that form as the spinor; see
\citef{hestenes2012clifford}. The remark records the homomorphism
when such an ideal is given. It does not assert that a minimal left
ideal exists for every quadratic form over every ring.}
